WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Around 1499, in Punjab, a young
man goes to bathe in a river.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.000
He disappears.

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.480
Three days later he returns.

4
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.850
Sikhs believe he was
taken into God's presence.

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.560
His first words are remembered
as: there is no Hindu,

6
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.270
there is no Muslim.

7
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.480
He is Guru Nanak, the first Guru.

8
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.340
Nine more Gurus follow him, until 1708.

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.700
So why do Sikhs say ten different
men were all the same Guru?

10
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.630
In this mission, you'll
follow Guru Nanak's life,

11
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.880
from the river to the
community he founded.

12
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.170
Then you'll meet the
tenth Guru, Gobind Singh,

13
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.850
at Anandpur in 1699.

14
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.110
Your mission: find out why Sikhs say ten
different men were all the same Guru.
